      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"hijacked\" is a pretty heavy word to use. if the prefrontal cortex is actually being bypassed like that, are we talking about a temporary state, or can these specific geometric rhythms cause long-term neurological priming? i'm trying to figure out if this is just a fleeting impulse or if they are essentially re-wiring how people perceive these brand stimuli over time.",
